(   - Adoption: Mandatory standard across Europe, India \(BIS SP 46:2003\), ISO member nations, and) Tj
T*
(   Commonwealth countries.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   2. Third Angle Projection System:) Tj
T*
(   - Principle: The object is placed in the Third Quadrant. The transparent projection plane is) Tj
T*
(   situated directly BETWEEN the observer and the object.) Tj
T*
(   - Projection Mechanics: The observer views the object through the transparent plane; the image) Tj
T*
(   is traced directly onto the surface facing the observer.) Tj
T*
(   - Arrangement of Views on Sheet:) Tj
T*
(   * Front View \(Elevation\) is the central reference.) Tj
T*
(   * Top View \(Plan\) is drawn ABOVE the front view.) Tj
T*
(   * Left Hand Side View is drawn on the LEFT of the front view.) Tj
T*
(   * Right Hand Side View is drawn on the RIGHT of the front view.) Tj
T*
(   * Bottom View is drawn BELOW the front view.) Tj
T*
(   - Graphical Symbol: Frustum of a cone with the two concentric circles positioned on the LEFT,) Tj
T*
(   and the trapezoidal profile on the RIGHT.) Tj
T*
(   - Adoption: Official industrial standard in USA and Canada \(ANSI/ASME Y14.3\) and widely used in) Tj
T*
(   automotive CAD.) Tj
T*
() Tj
