(   - Rule 3 \(Hidden T-Junctions\):) Tj
T*
(   When a hidden line intersects another hidden line forming a T, the cross dash must touch the) Tj
T*
(   stem dash solidly.) Tj
T*
(   - Rule 4 \(Crossing Hidden Lines\):) Tj
T*
(   When two non-intersecting hidden lines cross in projection \(one in front of the other in) Tj
T*
(   space\), one dash must bridge the gap of the other to prevent the appearance of a false 4-way) Tj
T*
(   intersection.) Tj
T*
(   - Rule 5 \(Parallel Adjacent Lines\):) Tj
T*
(   When a hidden line runs parallel and close to a visible line, stagger the dashes to prevent the) Tj
T*
(   appearance of a single blurred line.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   3. Omission Rule:) Tj
T*
(   Hidden lines should be omitted when they do not contribute to clarity or when a sectional view) Tj
T*
(   is provided that shows those features as visible outlines.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
