(>> Solution to Question 6:) Tj
T*
ET
BT
/F1 8.5 Tf
12.5 TL
(   [Problem Statement]: Describe the conventions for representing cylindrical features, circular holes, and pitch circle diameters in orthographic views, detailing centerlines and cross marks.) Tj
T*
(   [Detailed Step-by-Step Answer]:) Tj
T*
(   1. Geometric Representation of Cylinders:) Tj
T*
(   - A right circular cylinder appears as a true circle when viewed along its longitudinal axis,) Tj
T*
(   and as a rectangle when viewed perpendicular to its axis.) Tj
T*
(   - Axis Representation:) Tj
T*
(   * In the rectangular view, the axis of the cylinder MUST be shown by a Chain Thin Line \(Type G,) Tj
T*
(   long dash-dot: 10-12 mm dash, 1 mm space, 1.5 mm dot/short dash\).) Tj
T*
(   * The centerline must extend 2 mm to 5 mm past the outer boundary lines of the cylinder to) Tj
T*
(   indicate that the cylinder continues symmetrically.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   2. Representation of Circular Holes:) Tj
T*
(   - In the view parallel to the hole axis:) Tj
T*
(   * The hole appears as a circle. Its center is marked by two mutually perpendicular chain thin) Tj
T*
(   lines intersecting at their long dashes \(not at their dots or gaps!\).) Tj
T*
(   * For small holes \(diameter < 10 mm\), the centerline is simplified to two intersecting short) Tj
T*
(   continuous thin lines \(+ mark\).) Tj
T*
(   - In the view perpendicular to the hole axis:) Tj
T*
(   * The boundaries of the cylindrical hole are obscured by solid material and are drawn as two) Tj
T*
(   parallel Dashed Thin Lines \(hidden lines\) separated by the diameter.) Tj
T*
(   * The central axis is drawn as a chain thin centerline extending through both ends.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   3. Pitch Circle Diameter \(PCD\):) Tj
T*
(   - In circular flanges or gears with multiple concentric bolt holes:) Tj
T*
(   * The pitch circle is drawn as a circular Chain Thin Line passing through the centers of all) Tj
T*
(   holes.) Tj
T*
(   * Radial centerlines pass through each hole center, defining their angular pitch.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(--------------------------------------------------------------------------------) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
ET
BT
/F2 8.5 Tf
12.5 TL
