(   - Criterion 1 \(Maximum Shape Characteristic\):) Tj
T*
(   Select the viewing direction that reveals the most distinctive profile, primary contours,) Tj
T*
(   steps, tapers, and characteristic features of the part.) Tj
T*
(   - Criterion 2 \(Minimum Hidden Lines\):) Tj
T*
(   Orient the object such that the internal cavities, holes, and slots are visible from the front) Tj
T*
(   or situated such that the resulting views contain the minimum possible number of hidden dashed) Tj
T*
(   lines.) Tj
T*
(   - Criterion 3 \(Natural Operating Orientation\):) Tj
T*
(   Whenever practical, orient the object in the position it normally occupies in service or) Tj
T*
(   manufacturing \(e.g., motor shafts horizontal, engine pistons vertical, brackets seated on their) Tj
T*
(   mounting bases\).) Tj
T*
(   - Criterion 4 \(Longest Dimension Horizontal\):) Tj
T*
(   Position the longest linear dimension of the component horizontally. This utilizes the wide) Tj
T*
(   landscape format of standard engineering drawing sheets \(A4, A3, A2\) most efficiently.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   2. Practical Impact:) Tj
T*
(   A poorly chosen front view results in cluttered top and side views dominated by overlapping) Tj
T*
(   dashed lines, increasing drafting time, visual fatigue, and the likelihood of costly machining) Tj
T*
(   errors in the workshop.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(--------------------------------------------------------------------------------) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
