(>> Solution to Question 8:) Tj
T*
ET
BT
/F1 8.5 Tf
12.5 TL
(   [Problem Statement]: Explain the LINETYPE and LTSCALE commands in AutoCAD, discussing how linetype files \(.lin\) are structured, loaded, and scaled for model space and paper space layouts.) Tj
T*
(   [Detailed Step-by-Step Answer]:) Tj
T*
(   1. LINETYPE Command and Management:) Tj
T*
(   - Command: LINETYPE \(or 'LT' [Enter]\) opens the Linetype Manager dialog box.) Tj
T*
(   - By default, a new drawing contains only the 'Continuous' linetype.) Tj
T*
(   - Clicking 'Load' accesses the standard definitions file 'acadiso.lin' \(metric\) or 'acad.lin') Tj
T*
(   \(imperial\), allowing the user to load standard patterns:) Tj
T*
(   * HIDDEN: Standard dashed line \(dash 6 mm, space 3 mm\).) Tj
T*
(   * HIDDEN2: Half-scale dashed line.) Tj
T*
(   * CENTER: Standard centerline \(long dash 32 mm, space 6 mm, short dash 6 mm, space 6 mm\).) Tj
T*
(   * CENTER2: Half-scale centerline.) Tj
T*
(   * PHANTOM: Alternate position line \(long dash, space, short dash, space, short dash, space\).) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   2. Global Linetype Scale \(LTSCALE\):) Tj
T*
(   - Sets the global scaling factor applied to all linetypes in the drawing.) Tj
T*
(   - Command: LTSCALE [Enter] -> Enter new factor.) Tj
T*
(   - In 1:1 metric drafting on A3 sheets, setting LTSCALE = 0.5 to 1.0 ensures dashes display with) Tj
T*
(   crisp proportion.) Tj
T*
(   - If drawing in meter units, LTSCALE must be set to 500 to 1000 to prevent lines from appearing) Tj
T*
(   solid.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   3. Paper Space Scaling \(PSLTSCALE\):) Tj
T*
(   - Controls viewport linetype scaling in Paper Space layouts.) Tj
T*
(   - PSLTSCALE = 1: Automatically scales all linetypes based on sheet paper units so that dashes) Tj
T*
(   plot at identical physical lengths regardless of individual viewport zoom scales.) Tj
T*
(   - PSLTSCALE = 0: Linetype scale is governed purely by model space zoom factor.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(--------------------------------------------------------------------------------) Tj
