(   [Problem Statement]: Detail the TRIM and EXTEND commands in AutoCAD, explaining Cutting/Boundary edge selection, Standard vs Quick mode, and the Shift-key toggle behavior.) Tj
T*
(   [Detailed Step-by-Step Answer]:) Tj
T*
(   1. TRIM Command \(TR\):) Tj
T*
(   - Function: Cuts and deletes portions of an entity that extend beyond an intersecting boundary) Tj
T*
(   edge.) Tj
T*
(   - Modern AutoCAD Quick Mode \(Default\):) Tj
T*
(   * Executing 'TRIM' immediately treats ALL visible drawing entities as potential cutting edges!) Tj
T*
(   * Hovering cursor over any line segment previews the deletion with a red 'X'.) Tj
T*
(   * Clicking the segment or dragging a crossing line across multiple lines trims them instantly.) Tj
T*
(   - Standard Mode \(Select Cutting Edges\):) Tj
T*
(   * System variable TRIMMODE = 0 restores traditional behavior.) Tj
T*
(   * User explicitly selects cutting edge boundaries first, presses Enter, then clicks segments to) Tj
T*
(   trim.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   2. EXTEND Command \(EX\):) Tj
T*
(   - Function: Extends a line, arc, or open polyline until it terminates precisely at a boundary) Tj
T*
(   edge.) Tj
T*
(   - Quick Mode: Hovering near the end of a line previews its extension to the nearest boundary;) Tj
T*
(   clicking performs the extension.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   3. The Shift-Key Toggle Workflow:) Tj
T*
(   - While actively using the TRIM command, holding down the SHIFT key temporarily converts the) Tj
T*
(   command into EXTEND! Clicking an entity extends it to the next boundary.) Tj
T*
(   - Conversely, while actively using EXTEND, holding down SHIFT converts it into TRIM.) Tj
T*
(   - This toggle allows alternating between trimming and extending complex intersections without) Tj
T*
(   switching commands.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(--------------------------------------------------------------------------------) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
ET
