12.5 TL
(   [Problem Statement]: Explain the ARRAY command in AutoCAD, providing comprehensive mathematical and operational details for Rectangular Array, Polar Array, and Path Array.) Tj
T*
(   [Detailed Step-by-Step Answer]:) Tj
T*
(   1. Overview of the ARRAY Command \(AR\):) Tj
T*
(   - The ARRAY command creates regular, parametric patterns of selected objects distributed in 2D) Tj
T*
(   or 3D space.) Tj
T*
(   - Associativity: By default, arrays are created as 'Associative' compound objects. Selecting) Tj
T*
(   any element displays parametric ribbon panels and multi-functional editing grips.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   2. Rectangular Array:) Tj
T*
(   - Arranges elements in a grid pattern along rows \(Y-direction\) and columns \(X-direction\).) Tj
T*
(   - Parameters:) Tj
T*
(   * Column Count \(Nc\) and Column Spacing \(dx\): Center-to-center distance along X.) Tj
T*
(   * Row Count \(Nr\) and Row Spacing \(dy\): Center-to-center distance along Y.) Tj
T*
(   * Total span along X = \(Nc - 1\) * dx; Total span along Y = \(Nr - 1\) * dy.) Tj
T*
(   * Level Count & Level Spacing: Extends the array into 3D along Z-axis.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   3. Polar Array \(Radial / Circular Pattern\):) Tj
T*
(   - Arranges elements around a central pivot point along a circular trajectory.) Tj
T*
(   - Parameters:) Tj
T*
(   * Center Point: Coordinates of rotation axis.) Tj
T*
(   * Number of Items \(N\): Total instances created \(including original\).) Tj
T*
(   * Fill Angle: Angular sweep over which items are distributed \(default 360? for full circle;) Tj
T*
(   180? for semicircle\).) Tj
T*
(   * Angle Between Items = Fill Angle / \(N - 1\) or Fill Angle / N.) Tj
T*
(   * Rotate Items \(Y/N\): If Yes, elements rotate radially as they circle; if No, elements maintain) Tj
T*
(   their initial orientation.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   4. Path Array:) Tj
T*
(   - Distributes repeated objects along the trajectory of a selected path \(Line, Polyline, Arc,) Tj
T*
(   Spline, or Ellipse\).) Tj
T*
(   - Method Options:) Tj
T*
(   * Divide: Spreads a specified number of items evenly along total path length.) Tj
T*
ET

