(   [Problem Statement]: Detail the MIRROR and SCALE commands in AutoCAD, explaining symmetry axis definition, source object retention, base point selection, and proportional resizing.) Tj
T*
(   [Detailed Step-by-Step Answer]:) Tj
T*
(   1. MIRROR Command \(MI\):) Tj
T*
(   - Function: Creates a reverse, reflected copy of selected entities across a user-specified) Tj
T*
(   mirror line, essential for symmetrical engineering components \(shafts, pistons, brackets\).) Tj
T*
(   - Command Steps:) Tj
T*
(   * Command: MIRROR [Enter] -> Select objects -> [Enter].) Tj
T*
(   * 'Specify first point of mirror line:' -> Snap to symmetry centerline using OSNAP.) Tj
T*
(   * 'Specify second point of mirror line:' -> Snap to second point along centerline \(turn on) Tj
T*
(   Ortho F8 for vertical/horizontal symmetry\).) Tj
T*
(   * 'Erase source objects? [Yes/No] <N>:': Press Enter to retain both halves, creating a complete) Tj
T*
(   symmetrical drawing.) Tj
T*
(   - System Variable MIRRTEXT:) Tj
T*
(   * MIRRTEXT = 0 \(Default\): Text and dimension values retain their natural readable orientation) Tj
T*
(   without being flipped backwards.) Tj
T*
(   * MIRRTEXT = 1: Mirrors text characters backwards like a true optical reflection.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   2. SCALE Command \(SC\):) Tj
T*
(   - Function: Enlarges or shrinks selected geometry uniformly in X, Y, and Z axes about a fixed) Tj
T*
(   anchor base point.) Tj
T*
(   - Command Steps:) Tj
T*
(   * Command: SCALE [Enter] -> Select objects -> [Enter].) Tj
T*
(   * 'Specify base point:' -> Pick anchor vertex that will remain stationary during resizing.) Tj
T*
(   * 'Specify scale factor or [Copy/Reference] <1.0000>:':) Tj
T*
(   - Factor > 1 \(e.g. 2.0\) doubles dimensions.) Tj
T*
(   - Factor < 1 \(e.g. 0.5\) halves dimensions.) Tj
T*
(   - Copy \(C\): Generates a scaled duplicate, preserving original.) Tj
T*
(   - Reference \(R\): Scales geometry to match an explicit target dimension without calculating) Tj
T*
(   fractional multipliers.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(--------------------------------------------------------------------------------) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
