(   [Problem Statement]: A cast iron bearing bracket has a base 120 mm x 60 mm x 20 mm thick, a central vertical upright 60 mm wide x 20 mm thick x 50 mm high, and a horizontal cylindrical hole of 30 mm diameter drilled centrally through the upright. Provide a detailed step-by-step description of its Front View, Top View, and Right Hand Side View in First Angle Projection.) Tj
T*
(   [Detailed Step-by-Step Answer]:) Tj
T*
(   1. Component Breakdown and Geometry:) Tj
T*
(   - Base Plate: Width = 120 mm, Depth = 60 mm, Height = 20 mm.) Tj
T*
(   - Central Upright: Centered on base. Width = 60 mm \(from X = 30 to X = 90\), Depth = 20 mm) Tj
T*
(   \(centered on 60 mm depth, from Y = 20 to Y = 40\), Height = 50 mm above base \(Top Z = 20 + 50 =) Tj
T*
(   70 mm\).) Tj
T*
(   - Cylindrical Bore: Diameter = 30 mm. Axis is horizontal, parallel to X-axis \(drilled along) Tj
T*
(   length\), located at center of upright: Y = 30 mm, Z = 20 + 25 = 45 mm above bottom.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   2. Front View \(Looking along Y-direction, Width X vs Height Z\):) Tj
T*
(   - Base Plate: A horizontal rectangle 120 mm wide x 20 mm high.) Tj
T*
(   - Central Upright: A rectangle 60 mm wide x 50 mm high resting on top of the base plate between) Tj
T*
(   X = 30 and X = 90, rising to Z = 70 mm.) Tj
T*
(   - Cylindrical Hole: The hole penetrates through the 20 mm thickness of the upright. Since) Tj
T*
(   looking perpendicular to hole axis, it appears as two parallel Dashed Thin Lines spaced 30 mm) Tj
T*
(   apart \(at Z = 30 mm and Z = 60 mm\) spanning from X = 30 to X = 90.) Tj
T*
(   - Centerline: A chain thin horizontal line along Z = 45 mm.) Tj
T*
(   - Overall Boundary: Stepped profile of width 120 mm and height 70 mm.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   3. Top View \(Looking vertically downward from above, Width X vs Depth Y\):) Tj
T*
(   - Base Plate: An outer rectangle 120 mm wide x 60 mm deep.) Tj
T*
(   - Central Upright: A rectangle 60 mm wide x 20 mm deep located symmetrically in the center) Tj
T*
(   \(from X = 30 to 90, and Y = 20 to 40\).) Tj
T*
(   - Cylindrical Hole: Obscured from above. Shown as two parallel Dashed Thin Lines spaced 30 mm) Tj
T*
(   apart \(at Y = 15 and Y = 45\) spanning through the upright between X = 30 and X = 90.) Tj
T*
(   - Centerline: A chain thin horizontal line along Y = 30 mm.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   4. Right Hand Side View \(Looking from the Right, drawn on the LEFT of Front View in First) Tj
T*
(   Angle\):) Tj
T*
(   - Base Plate: A rectangle 60 mm wide \(depth\) x 20 mm high.) Tj
T*
(   - Upright: A rectangle 20 mm wide x 50 mm high centered on top of base \(from Y = 20 to 40,) Tj
T*
(   rising to Z = 70 mm\).) Tj
T*
(   - Cylindrical Hole: Seen end-on along its axis! Appears as a visible TRUE CIRCLE of diameter 30) Tj
T*
(   mm with center at Y = 30 mm, Z = 45 mm, marked with intersecting centerlines \(+\).) Tj
T*
() Tj
