(   [Problem Statement]: Explain the procedure to convert an isometric pictorial drawing of a stepped machine block with a V-groove and countersunk hole into complete orthographic views in AutoCAD.) Tj
T*
(   [Detailed Step-by-Step Answer]:) Tj
T*
(   AutoCAD Drafting Sequence:) Tj
T*
(   1. Environment Setup:) Tj
T*
(   - Units: Decimal, Millimeters. Limits: 0,0 to 420,297 \(A3\). ZOOM ALL.) Tj
T*
(   - Create Layers: 'VISIBLE' \(0.5 mm\), 'HIDDEN' \(0.25 mm, HIDDEN\), 'CENTER' \(0.25 mm, CENTER\),) Tj
T*
(   'CONSTRUCT' \(0.18 mm, Continuous\), 'DIM' \(0.25 mm\).) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   2. Draft Front View \(Anchor View\):) Tj
T*
(   - Switch to 'VISIBLE' layer.) Tj
T*
(   - Command: LINE -> Draw base line: 0,150 to @100<0.) Tj
T*
(   - Draw stepped vertical outlines, top horizontal plateau, and sloping V-groove boundaries using) Tj
T*
(   relative polar entries \(e.g. @25<-45, @25<45\).) Tj
T*
(   - Draw through-hole and countersunk boundaries as dashed hidden lines on layer 'HIDDEN':) Tj
T*
(   * Command: LINE -> Specify start point -> Draw hidden vertical walls of hole.) Tj
T*
(   * Draw 90? countersunk bevel lines at top surface.) Tj
T*
(   - Add chain thin centerline on layer 'CENTER'.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   3. Project Top View:) Tj
T*
(   - Switch to 'CONSTRUCT' layer. Turn on Ortho \(F8\).) Tj
T*
(   - Command: LINE -> Project vertical construction rays downwards from every vertex, corner, and) Tj
T*
(   center in the Front View.) Tj
T*
(   - Switch to 'VISIBLE' layer. Draw top view horizontal boundary lines at appropriate depth) Tj
T*
(   offset \(e.g. Y = 50 to Y = 110\).) Tj
T*
(   - Trim intersection lines using TRIM \(TR\).) Tj
T*
(   - Where the V-groove passes across the block, draw visible horizontal boundary edges.) Tj
T*
(   - For countersunk hole: Draw two concentric circles using CIRCLE \(Center, Radius\) on layer) Tj
T*
(   'VISIBLE':) Tj
T*
(   * Inner circle = Through-hole diameter.) Tj
T*
(   * Outer circle = Countersink outer diameter. Add cross centerlines.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   4. Construct Side View via 45? Miter Line:) Tj
T*
(   - On 'CONSTRUCT' layer, draw horizontal line from bottom of Front View and vertical line from) Tj
T*
(   right of Top View intersecting at origin O.) Tj
T*
(   - Command: LINE -> From O, draw miter ray: @150<45.) Tj
T*
(   - Project all depth features from Top View horizontally to miter line, then vertically upward) Tj
T*
(   into Side View.) Tj
T*
(   - Project height features horizontally from Front View to intersect vertical projectors.) Tj
T*
(   - Connect visible outlines on 'VISIBLE' layer; convert internal obscured cavities to 'HIDDEN') Tj
T*
(   layer.) Tj
T*
(   - Turn off or freeze 'CONSTRUCT' layer for clean presentation.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(--------------------------------------------------------------------------------) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
ET
