(   [Problem Statement]: Discuss the representation of intersections of curved surfaces in orthographic projection, detailing the line of intersection between two intersecting cylinders of equal and unequal diameters.) Tj
T*
(   [Detailed Step-by-Step Answer]:) Tj
T*
(   1. Intersection of Two Cylinders of UNEQUAL Diameters:) Tj
T*
(   - Configuration: A vertical main cylinder of large diameter D is penetrated horizontally by a) Tj
T*
(   smaller branch cylinder of diameter d \(d < D\) such that their axes intersect perpendicularly.) Tj
T*
(   - Nature of Intersection:) Tj
T*
(   * In the top view, the intersection points lie on the circular circumference of the large) Tj
T*
(   cylinder.) Tj
T*
(   * In the side view, the intersection is seen on the circular profile of the small cylinder.) Tj
T*
