(   * In the Front View, the intersection forms a smooth 3D spatial curve \(hyperbolic curve\) convex) Tj
T*
(   towards the axis of the larger cylinder.) Tj
T*
(   - Plotting Method \(Cutting Plane Method\):) Tj
T*
(   * Pass multiple horizontal cutting planes through both cylinders.) Tj
T*
(   * Each horizontal cutting plane cuts two straight line generators from the small cylinder and a) Tj
T*
(   circular arc from the large cylinder.) Tj
T*
(   * The intersection of these generators with the circle gives discrete points on the) Tj
T*
(   intersection curve.) Tj
T*
(   * Plot these points in the Front View and connect with a smooth curve using a French Curve or) Tj
T*
(   AutoCAD SPLINE.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   2. Intersection of Two Cylinders of EQUAL Diameters \(d = D\):) Tj
T*
(   - When two right circular cylinders of identical diameter intersect with their axes at 90) Tj
T*
(   degrees, the 3D intersection curve degenerates into two planar intersecting ellipses!) Tj
T*
(   - In the Front View, these two intersecting ellipses project as two STRAIGHT LINES intersecting) Tj
T*
(   at the center like an 'X'!) Tj
T*
(   - This is an extremely common drafting convention in piping tees and manifold junctions.) Tj
T*
