(   [Problem Statement]: Explain the methods of creating and editing rectangular arrays in AutoCAD using both the command-line interface and the contextual Ribbon Array tab.) Tj
T*
(   [Detailed Step-by-Step Answer]:) Tj
T*
(   1. Command-Line Creation of Rectangular Array:) Tj
T*
(   - Command: -ARRAY \(or ARRAYCLASSIC\)) Tj
T*
(   - Prompt: Select objects -> Pick entities -> [Enter].) Tj
T*
(   - Enter array type: [Rectangular/Polar] -> Type 'R' [Enter].) Tj
T*
(   - Enter number of rows \(---\) <1>: Enter row count Nr \(e.g. 4\).) Tj
T*
(   - Enter number of columns \(|||\) <1>: Enter column count Nc \(e.g. 6\).) Tj
T*
(   - Enter distance between rows: Enter row spacing dy \(positive = upward, negative = downward\).) Tj
T*
(   - Enter distance between columns: Enter column spacing dx \(positive = rightward, negative =) Tj
T*
(   leftward\).) Tj
T*
(   - AutoCAD generates a 4x6 grid of 24 instances.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   2. Contextual Ribbon Array Tab:) Tj
T*
(   - When an Associative Array is created or selected in modern AutoCAD, the Ribbon automatically) Tj
T*
(   switches to the 'Array Creation / Array Editor' tab:) Tj
T*
(   * Columns Panel: Direct numeric text boxes for Columns count, Between distance, and Total span.) Tj
T*
(   * Rows Panel: Rows count, Between distance, Total span, and Incrementing elevation.) Tj
T*
(   * Levels Panel: 3D stacking along Z-axis.) Tj
T*
(   * Properties Panel: Associative toggle button, Base Point relocation button.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   3. In-Canvas Grip Editing:) Tj
T*
(   - Hovering or clicking grips on the associative array allows dynamic manipulation:) Tj
T*
(   * Square Base Grip: Moves the entire array.) Tj
T*
(   * Triangular Axis Grips: Dynamically drag to adjust row/column spacing interactively.) Tj
T*
(   * Corner Arrow Grip: Drag to increase or decrease both row and column counts simultaneously.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(--------------------------------------------------------------------------------) Tj
T*
() Tj
