(   [Problem Statement]: A stepped shaft has three concentric cylindrical sections: Section 1 \(diameter 60 mm, length 40 mm\), Section 2 \(diameter 40 mm, length 60 mm\), and Section 3 \(diameter 25 mm, length 50 mm\). Section 2 has a central keyway 10 mm wide x 4 mm deep x 30 mm long. Describe its Front View and End View in First Angle projection.) Tj
T*
(   [Detailed Step-by-Step Answer]:) Tj
T*
(   1. Component Architecture:) Tj
T*
(   - Concentric stepped shaft aligned with horizontal axis \(X-axis\).) Tj
T*
(   - Section 1: Diameter D1 = 60 mm, Length L1 = 40 mm \(from X = 0 to 40\).) Tj
T*
(   - Section 2: Diameter D2 = 40 mm, Length L2 = 60 mm \(from X = 40 to 100\).) Tj
T*
(   - Section 3: Diameter D3 = 25 mm, Length L3 = 50 mm \(from X = 100 to 150\).) Tj
T*
(   - Total length = 40 + 60 + 50 = 150 mm.) Tj
T*
(   - Keyway in Section 2: Width W = 10 mm, Depth T = 4 mm, Length = 30 mm \(centered from X = 55 to) Tj
T*
(   85, milled into top surface at Y = 0, Z = +20 to +16\).) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   2. Front View \(Horizontal Axis Elevation\):) Tj
T*
(   - Centerline: A continuous chain thin line along the horizontal center of symmetry \(Z = 0\).) Tj
T*
(   - Section 1: A rectangle 40 mm wide x 60 mm high \(Z from -30 to +30\).) Tj
T*
(   - Section 2: A rectangle 60 mm wide x 40 mm high \(Z from -20 to +20\).) Tj
T*
(   - Section 3: A rectangle 50 mm wide x 25 mm high \(Z from -12.5 to +12.5\).) Tj
T*
(   - Keyway Representation:) Tj
T*
(   * The keyway is cut into the top surface of Section 2.) Tj
T*
(   * Since looking from the front, the bottom floor of the keyway is obscured.) Tj
T*
(   * It appears as a horizontal Dashed Thin Line of length 30 mm \(from X = 55 to 85\) located 4 mm) Tj
T*
(   below the top edge of Section 2 \(at Z = 20 - 4 = 16 mm\).) Tj
T*
(   * The ends of the keyway are terminated by vertical dashed lines.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
