(   2. Conventional Representation Rules:) Tj
T*
(   - Rule 1 \(Omission of Line\):) Tj
T*
(   Where a flat planar surface blends tangentially into a cylinder, cone, or fillet curve, NO LINE) Tj
T*
(   is drawn on the orthographic view representing that transition.) Tj
T*
(   - Rule 2 \(Runout Curves\):) Tj
T*
(   Where a filleted corner intersects or terminates at a curved contoured body \(e.g., a web or rib) Tj
T*
(   joining a cylindrical boss\), the intersection line fades out.) Tj
T*
(   Conventionally, this transition is represented by a partial circular arc or curve called a) Tj
T*
(   'Runout'.) Tj
T*
(   The runout curve terminates tangentially before reaching the main outer boundary.) Tj
T*
(   - Rule 3 \(Fictitious Lines of Intersection\):) Tj
T*
(   For clarity on complex castings, draftsmen historically used thin continuous lines \(~0.25 mm\)) Tj
T*
(   stopping slightly short of outer contours to delineate major structural flanges that have) Tj
T*
(   rounded corners.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
