(   [Problem Statement]: Detail the STRETCH command in AutoCAD, explaining crossing-window selection rules, vertex translation, and how to resize multi-view orthographic features consistently.) Tj
T*
(   [Detailed Step-by-Step Answer]:) Tj
T*
(   1. Purpose of the STRETCH Command \(S\):) Tj
T*
(   - The STRETCH command elongates or shortens portions of a drawing while maintaining the) Tj
T*
(   connectivity of all attached lines, polylines, arcs, and dimension extension lines.) Tj
T*
(   - Unlike SCALE \(which multiplies all dimensions\), STRETCH displaces selected vertices linearly) Tj
T*
(   along a vector without altering unselected vertices.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   2. Mandatory Crossing Selection Rule:) Tj
T*
(   - STRETCH operates STRICTLY via Crossing Window \(C\) or Crossing Polygon \(CP\) selection:) Tj
T*
(   * Entities COMPLETELY ENCLOSED within the crossing window are MOVED bodily.) Tj
T*
(   * Entities CROSSED by the boundary of the window have their crossed vertices moved while their) Tj
T*
(   opposite uncrossed vertices remain pinned in place!) Tj
T*
(   * Entities outside the window are completely unaffected.) Tj
T*
(   - Selecting objects via standard Window \(blue box\) or direct clicking converts STRETCH into) Tj
T*
(   standard MOVE.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   3. Consistent Multi-View Resizing Scenario:) Tj
T*
(   - Suppose a shaft's length must be increased by 25 mm across Front View, Top View, and) Tj
T*
(   associated dimension lines:) Tj
T*
(   * Command: STRETCH [Enter]) Tj
T*
(   * Drag a Crossing Window from bottom-right to top-left enclosing the right ends of BOTH the) Tj
T*
(   Front View and Top View simultaneously.) Tj
T*
(   * Specify base point -> Turn on Ortho \(F8\) -> Drag mouse cursor to the right -> Type '25') Tj
T*
(   [Enter].) Tj
T*
(   * Both views and associative dimensions stretch by exactly 25 mm simultaneously, perfectly) Tj
T*
(   preserving orthographic alignment!) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(--------------------------------------------------------------------------------) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
ET
BT
/F2 8.5 Tf
12.5 TL
