(   2. Baseline Dimensioning \(DIMBASELINE - DBL\):) Tj
T*
(   - Function: Creates a series of parallel dimensions originating from a single common reference) Tj
T*
(   datum edge.) Tj
T*
(   - Advantage: Eliminates cumulative manufacturing tolerances; each feature location is machined) Tj
T*
(   independently from the primary datum surface.) Tj
T*
(   - Command Sequence: Place initial dimension via DIMLINEAR -> Execute DIMBASELINE -> Click) Tj
T*
(   subsequent feature edges. AutoCAD offsets each dimension line by the preset baseline spacing) Tj
T*
(   automatically.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   3. Continuous \(Chain\) Dimensioning \(DIMCONTINUE - DCO\):) Tj
T*
(   - Function: Places dimensions in a continuous end-to-end series along a single straight line.) Tj
T*
(   - Application: Used where the overall length is non-critical, or where step-to-step spacing is) Tj
T*
(   functionally paramount.) Tj
T*
(   - Precaution: Never dimension every segment in a closed chain and also provide the overall) Tj
T*
(   dimension; omit one non-critical segment to prevent tolerance conflicts.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(--------------------------------------------------------------------------------) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
