12.5 TL
(   [Problem Statement]: A hollow hexagonal prism \(base side 40 mm, height 80 mm, central circular hole of diameter 35 mm through its length\) rests on its base on HP with one base edge parallel to VP. Describe its orthographic Front View, Top View, and Left Hand Side View in First Angle projection.) Tj
T*
(   [Detailed Step-by-Step Answer]:) Tj
T*
(   1. Solid Geometry:) Tj
T*
(   - Regular hexagonal prism of outer base edge s = 40 mm, axis height H = 80 mm.) Tj
T*
(   - Axis is vertical \(perpendicular to HP, parallel to VP\).) Tj
T*
(   - One base edge is parallel to VP.) Tj
T*
(   - Central axial cylindrical hole of diameter D = 35 mm drilled completely from top to bottom.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   2. Top View \(Looking downward from above, on HP\):) Tj
T*
(   - Outer Boundary: A regular hexagon of side 40 mm.) Tj
T*
(   * Two edges are horizontal \(parallel to XY line\) of length 40 mm.) Tj
T*
(   * Distance between parallel flats: W_flats = s * sqrt\(3\) = 40 * 1.732 = 69.28 mm.) Tj
T*
(   * Corner-to-corner major diagonal = 2 * s = 80 mm.) Tj
T*
(   - Central Hole: A concentric visible circle of diameter 35 mm on layer 'VISIBLE' with cross) Tj
T*
(   centerlines \(+\).) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   3. Front View \(Elevation on VP, looking parallel to base edge\):) Tj
T*
(   - Outer Boundary: A rectangle of width equal to corner-to-corner diagonal \(80 mm\) and height 80) Tj
T*
(   mm.) Tj
T*
(   - Vertical Visible Edges: Three visible vertical faces are shown separated by two vertical) Tj
T*
(   lines \(Type A\) representing the front corners, positioned at distance 20 mm from the outer) Tj
T*
(   edges.) Tj
T*
(   - Central Hole: Obscured from the front. Represented by two vertical Dashed Thin Lines spaced) Tj
T*
(   35 mm apart \(17.5 mm on either side of central vertical centerline\) extending through the full) Tj
T*
(   80 mm height.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   4. Left Hand Side View \(Drawn on RIGHT of Front View in First Angle\):) Tj
T*
(   - Width of Side View = distance between parallel flats = 69.28 mm.) Tj
T*
