(   [Problem Statement]: Explain the methods of creating and managing AutoCAD Blocks \(BLOCK, BMAKE, WBLOCK, INSERT\) for standard orthographic symbols and hardware components.) Tj
T*
(   [Detailed Step-by-Step Answer]:) Tj
T*
(   1. Concept and Purpose of Blocks:) Tj
T*
(   - A Block is a named collection of drawing entities grouped together to act as a single) Tj
T*
(   reusable library component \(e.g. projection symbols, bolts, bearings, title blocks\).) Tj
T*
(   - Advantages: Reduces file size \(database stores geometry once, multiple insertions store only) Tj
T*
(   insertion coordinates and scale\), speeds up drafting, enables global attribute updates.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   2. Creating Internal Blocks \(BLOCK / BMAKE\):) Tj
T*
(   - Command: BLOCK \(or 'B' [Enter]\) opens Block Definition dialog.) Tj
T*
(   - 1. Name: Assign unique descriptive name \(e.g., 'SYM_1ST_ANGLE'\).) Tj
T*
(   - 2. Base Point: Click 'Pick point' to select insertion origin \(e.g. geometric center or) Tj
T*
(   mounting corner\).) Tj
T*
(   - 3. Objects: Click 'Select objects' -> Window the drawn symbol entities. Choose 'Convert to) Tj
T*
(   block' or 'Retain'.) Tj
T*
(   - 4. Settings: Check 'Allow exploding' and select unit 'Millimeters'. Click OK.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   3. Creating External Block Libraries \(WBLOCK - Write Block\):) Tj
T*
(   - Command: WBLOCK [Enter] exports a block or selected geometry as an independent .dwg file on) Tj
T*
(   the hard drive.) Tj
T*
(   - Enables sharing across different project drawings and design teams.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   4. Inserting Blocks \(INSERT - I\):) Tj
T*
(   - Command: INSERT opens the Blocks Palette.) Tj
T*
(   - Drag and drop block into drawing canvas.) Tj
T*
(   - Prompts for Insertion Point, X/Y Scale factor \(default 1.0\), and Rotation angle \(default 0?\).) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(--------------------------------------------------------------------------------) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
