/F1 8.5 Tf
12.5 TL
(   [Problem Statement]: Explain the use of construction lines \(XLINE and RAY\) in AutoCAD for establishing multi-view projection alignments, detailing their infinite geometry and sub-options.) Tj
T*
(   [Detailed Step-by-Step Answer]:) Tj
T*
(   1. Concept of Infinite Construction Rays:) Tj
T*
(   - In manual drafting, projectors are drawn lightly with 4H pencils and erased later. In) Tj
T*
(   AutoCAD, XLINE and RAY provide electronic construction lines of infinite mathematical length) Tj
T*
(   that span across the viewport.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   2. XLINE Command \(Construction Line - XL\):) Tj
T*
(   - Function: Creates an infinite straight line passing through both directions from a point.) Tj
T*
(   - Sub-Options:) Tj
T*
(   * Hor \(H\): Creates an infinite horizontal line at picked Y-coordinate. Ideal for projecting) Tj
T*
(   heights between Front View and Side Views.) Tj
T*
(   * Ver \(V\): Creates an infinite vertical line at picked X-coordinate. Ideal for projecting) Tj
T*
(   widths between Front View and Top View.) Tj
T*
(   * Ang \(A\): Creates an infinite line at specified angle \(e.g. 45? for miter lines\) or reference) Tj
T*
ET

